VeridianOS: fix plasma5support compiler warnings (deprecations, sign-compare, unused parameter)

GCC reported, and this change fixes:

- dataengineconsumer.cpp: -Wunused-parameter 'job'. The parameter is used
  only inside the #ifndef NDEBUG block, so release builds never read it; it
  is now [[maybe_unused]]. The slot signature (connected by SIGNAL/SLOT
  string) is unchanged.
- datamodel.cpp: QSortFilterProxyModel::invalidateFilter() is deprecated
  (Qt 6.13). Ported to the documented replacement: beginFilterChange()
  before the filter callback is replaced, endFilterChange() after it
  (default Direction::Both, which is what invalidateFilter() did). One
  difference: beginFilterChange() builds the proxy's root
  mapping if it does not exist yet (filterAcceptsRow() over all source
  rows); if the proxy had not been queried yet, endFilterChange() then
  reports the difference as rowsRemoved/rowsInserted where
  invalidateFilter() emitted nothing. The resulting rows are the same.
- ion_noaa.cpp: QString::count() is deprecated; use size() (identical).
- datasource.cpp: QQmlPropertyMap(QObject *) is deprecated; use the
  documented QQmlPropertyMap::create(parent) factory (same object, same
  parent).
- ion_wettercom.cpp: QDateTime::fromSecsSinceEpoch(qint64, Qt::TimeSpec)
  is deprecated; pass QTimeZone::LocalTime instead of Qt::LocalTime (same
  local-time result).
- powermanagementjob.cpp: -Wsign-compare at the two "cookie != -1" checks.
  The cookies are uint and -1 meant "no inhibition active" (it converted to
  UINT_MAX, so the code worked). A named constant NoInhibitionCookie =
  std::numeric_limits<uint>::max() now replaces every use of -1 for these
  cookies (initialisers, checks, resets), so the sentinel is the same value
  and behaviour is unchanged.

Not handled here: "'TRANSLATION_DOMAIN' redefined" (0001).

